Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: bq256xx: the charge-limit supply is not a system battery

The driver registers a second supply, "bq256xx-battery", of type Battery
that reports only the charger's constant-charge current and voltage
limits. It has no capacity, energy or status. On a board whose real
battery is reported by a fuel gauge (the MANGMI Air X: the gauge's
"battery" supply), UPower takes the bq256xx one for a second system
battery, reads it as present and empty, and averages it into the display
device: OpenGamepadUI showed 50% and charging on a full battery, and its
docked/undocked performance profiles keyed off the wrong state.

Report POWER_SUPPLY_SCOPE_DEVICE for it. UPower then does not count it as
a system battery (scope "device"), and the kernel's own
power_supply_is_system_supplied() already skips device-scope supplies.
The charge-limit properties are unchanged.

---
 drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c
@@ -1228,6 +1228,17 @@
 
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CONSTANT_CHARGE_VOLTAGE_MAX:
 		val->intval = bq->init_data.vbatreg_max;
+		break;
+
+	/*
+	 * This supply only carries the charger's charge limits; it knows
+	 * nothing about the cell's state. The battery the system runs on is
+	 * the fuel gauge's supply. Without a scope, userspace (UPower) takes
+	 * this one for a second, empty system battery and averages it into
+	 * the displayed charge.
+	 */
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_SCOPE:
+		val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_SCOPE_DEVICE;
 		break;
 
 	default:
@@ -1663,6 +1674,7 @@
 static enum power_supply_property bq256xx_battery_props[] = {
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CONSTANT_CHARGE_CURRENT_MAX,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CONSTANT_CHARGE_VOLTAGE_MAX,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_SCOPE,
 };
 
 static int bq256xx_property_is_writeable(struct power_supply *psy,
